<!-- wp:group {"className":"fr-wrap fr-guide-intro","layout":{"type":"default"},"tagName":"section"} --><section class="wp-block-group fr-wrap fr-guide-intro"><!-- wp:group {"className":"fr-guide-opening","layout":{"type":"default"}} --><div class="wp-block-group fr-guide-opening"><!-- wp:group {"className":"fr-guide-opening-copy","layout":{"type":"default"}} --><div class="wp-block-group fr-guide-opening-copy"><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"fr-breadcrumb"} --><p class="fr-breadcrumb"><a class="text-link" href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/' ) ); ?>">Home</a> / Learn the Rosary</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading {"level":1} --><h1 class="wp-block-heading">How to pray<br>the Rosary</h1><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"fr-lead"} --><p class="fr-lead">The prayers. The beads. The mysteries.<br>A guide you can follow as you pray.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The Rosary brings prayer and reflection together. Follow the life of Jesus with Mary through five mysteries, with one decade of prayer for each.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:group {"className":"fr-actions","layout":{"type":"default"}} --><div class="wp-block-group fr-actions"><!-- wp:button {"className":"is-style-fill"} --><div class="wp-block-button is-style-fill"><a class="wp-block-button__link wp-element-button" href="#guided-prayer">Pray with the words</a></div><!-- /wp:button --><!-- wp:button {"className":"is-style-outline"} --><div class="wp-block-button is-style-outline"><a class="wp-block-button__link wp-element-button" href="#steps">Learn the steps</a></div><!-- /wp:button --><!-- wp:button {"className":"is-style-outline"} --><div class="wp-block-button is-style-outline"><a class="wp-block-button__link wp-element-button" href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/rosary-prayer-guide/' ) ); ?>">Print a guide</a></div><!-- /wp:button --></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"fr-small"} --><p class="fr-small">Jump to <a class="text-link" href="#prayer-words-complete">Rosary prayers in English</a>, <a class="text-link" href="#mysteries">mysteries by day</a> or <a class="text-link" href="#questions">questions about praying the Rosary</a>.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:group {"className":"fr-guide-beads","layout":{"type":"default"}} --><div class="wp-block-group fr-guide-beads"><!-- wp:html --><div class="fr-sacred-rosary" data-rosary-stage="intro" role="img" aria-label="A three-dimensional rosary with five decades, opening beads and a cross."><img class="fr-rosary-fallback" src="<?php echo esc_url( get_theme_file_uri( 'assets/cinema/through-mysteries.png' ) ); ?>" alt="A Catholic cross on a blue surface."/><div class="fr-rosary-stage-caption"><strong>One prayer. One bead.</strong><span>Cross, one bead, three beads, one bead, then five decades.</span></div></div><!-- /wp:html --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:html --><nav class="fr-jump" aria-label="On this page"><a href="#steps">The steps</a><a href="#guided-prayer">Pray the Rosary</a><a href="#prayer-words-complete">Prayer words</a><a href="#mysteries">The mysteries</a><a href="#questions">Your questions</a></nav><!-- /wp:html --></section><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:group {"className":"fr-wrap fr-section fr-guide-steps","layout":{"type":"default"},"tagName":"section","anchor":"steps"} --><section id="steps" class="wp-block-group fr-wrap fr-section fr-guide-steps"><!-- wp:group {"className":"fr-guide-aside","layout":{"type":"default"}} --><div class="wp-block-group fr-guide-aside"><!-- wp:heading {"level":2} --><h2 class="wp-block-heading">The steps, simply.</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>You don’t have to memorize everything first. Keep a guide nearby and pray at a pace that lets you reflect.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p><a class="text-link" href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/rosary-prayer-guide/' ) ); ?>">Read or print the complete guide</a></p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:group {"className":"fr-step-list","layout":{"type":"default"}} --><div class="wp-block-group fr-step-list"><!-- wp:group {"className":"fr-step","layout":{"type":"default"}} --><div class="wp-block-group fr-step"><!-- wp:heading {"level":3} --><h3 class="wp-block-heading">Begin with the opening prayers</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Make the Sign of the Cross and pray the Apostles’ Creed. Pray one Our Father, three Hail Marys, then the Glory Be.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:group {"className":"fr-step","layout":{"type":"default"}} --><div class="wp-block-group fr-step"><!-- wp:heading {"level":3} --><h3 class="wp-block-heading">Name the first mystery</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Bring the mystery to mind and offer your intention. Pray an Our Father, ten Hail Marys and the Glory Be while reflecting. Many people add the Fatima Prayer.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:group {"className":"fr-step","layout":{"type":"default"}} --><div class="wp-block-group fr-step"><!-- wp:heading {"level":3} --><h3 class="wp-block-heading">Continue through five decades</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Repeat the pattern for each of the remaining four mysteries. Each decade is ten Hail Marys, with an Our Father before and a Glory Be after.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:group {"className":"fr-step","layout":{"type":"default"}} --><div class="wp-block-group fr-step"><!-- wp:heading {"level":3} --><h3 class="wp-block-heading">Close in prayer</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>After five decades, pray the Hail, Holy Queen and the concluding prayer, then make the Sign of the Cross. The opening and closing prayer words are included below. The ministry’s printable guide offers another way to follow along.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div><!-- /wp:group --></section><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:html -->
<section id="guided-prayer" class="fr-wrap fr-section fr-prayer-tool fr-rosary-world" aria-labelledby="guided-prayer-heading">
<div class="fr-prayer-settings"><h2 id="guided-prayer-heading">Begin at the cross.<br>Pray the whole Rosary.</h2><p>Follow the prayers at your own pace. One person may lead, others may respond or listen quietly.</p>
<label class="fr-field" for="mystery-set">Mysteries<select id="mystery-set"><option value="joyful">Joyful</option><option value="sorrowful">Sorrowful</option><option value="glorious">Glorious</option><option value="luminous">Luminous</option></select></label>
<div class="fr-sacred-rosary fr-reader-rosary" data-rosary-stage="reader" aria-hidden="true"><img class="fr-rosary-fallback" src="<?php echo esc_url( get_theme_file_uri( 'assets/cinema/through-mysteries.png' ) ); ?>" alt=""/></div>
<fieldset class="fr-rosary-materials"><legend>Choose your beads</legend><button type="button" data-rosary-material="cobalt" aria-pressed="true">Cobalt</button><button type="button" data-rosary-material="wood" aria-pressed="false">Wood</button><button type="button" data-rosary-material="crystal" aria-pressed="false">Crystal</button></fieldset><p class="fr-small">Tap a bead to find its prayer, or use the prayer controls. Your place stays still until you move it.</p></div>
<div class="fr-prayer-reader" data-prayer-reader><p class="fr-prayer-mystery" id="prayer-mystery">Begin at the cross</p><p id="prayer-reference">Bring an intention, or hold it quietly in your heart.</p>
<div class="fr-prayer-progress"><span id="prayer-progress-text">Opening · Sign of the Cross</span><progress id="prayer-progress" aria-labelledby="prayer-progress-text" max="76" value="0">Opening prayers</progress></div>
<h3 id="prayer-title" tabindex="-1">The Sign of the Cross</h3><p class="fr-prayer-words" id="prayer-words">In the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit. Amen.</p>
<div class="fr-reader-controls"><button type="button" id="prayer-back" disabled>Previous prayer</button><button type="button" class="fr-primary" id="prayer-next">Next prayer</button></div>
<details class="fr-rosary-navigation"><summary>Choose a prayer</summary><div class="fr-rosary-choices"><label class="fr-field" for="prayer-phase">Go to a part<select id="prayer-phase"><option value="opening">Opening prayers</option><option value="decade">Five mysteries</option><option value="closing">Closing prayers</option></select></label><label class="fr-field" for="mystery-number">Choose a mystery<select id="mystery-number" disabled><option value="0">First mystery</option></select></label><label class="fr-field" for="prayer-jump">Find a prayer<select id="prayer-jump"><option value="0">Opening · Sign of the Cross</option></select></label></div></details>
<p class="fr-rosary-resume" id="prayer-resume" hidden></p><button type="button" class="fr-reset" id="prayer-reset">Start the Rosary again</button><p id="prayer-status" class="fr-sr-only" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><noscript><p>Read all the prayer words below and follow the steps above. The full Rosary remains available without interactive controls.</p></noscript></div></section>
<!-- /wp:html --><!-- wp:group {"className":"fr-wrap fr-section fr-reading fr-prayer-texts","layout":{"type":"default"},"tagName":"section","anchor":"prayer-words-complete"} --><section id="prayer-words-complete" class="wp-block-group fr-wrap fr-section fr-reading fr-prayer-texts"><!-- wp:heading {"level":2} --><h2 class="wp-block-heading">Rosary prayers in English</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Begin with the Sign of the Cross, the Apostles’ Creed, one Our Father, three Hail Marys and the Glory Be. For each decade, pray one Our Father, ten Hail Marys and the Glory Be. After the five decades, pray the Hail, Holy Queen and close with the Sign of the Cross. The concluding prayer is included below, alongside the prayers for each decade.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:details {"showContent":true} --><details class="wp-block-details" open><summary>The Sign of the Cross</summary><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>In the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit. Amen.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></details><!-- /wp:details --><!-- wp:details --><details class="wp-block-details"><summary>The Apostles’ Creed</summary><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>I believe in God, the Father Almighty, creator of heaven and earth, and in Jesus Christ, his only Son, our Lord, who was conceived by the Holy Spirit, born of the Virgin Mary, suffered under Pontius Pilate, was crucified, died and was buried; he descended into hell; on the third day he rose again from the dead; he ascended into heaven, and is seated at the right hand of God the Father Almighty; from there he will come again to judge the living and the dead. I believe in the Holy Spirit, the holy catholic Church, the communion of saints, the forgiveness of sins, the resurrection of the body, and life everlasting. Amen.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></details><!-- /wp:details --><!-- wp:details --><details class="wp-block-details"><summary>Our Father</summary><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Our Father, who art in heaven, hallowed be thy name; thy kingdom come; thy will be done on earth as it is in heaven. Give us this day our daily bread; and forgive us our trespasses, as we forgive those who trespass against us; and lead us not into temptation, but deliver us from evil. Amen.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></details><!-- /wp:details --><!-- wp:details --><details class="wp-block-details"><summary>Hail Mary</summary><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Hail Mary, full of grace, the Lord is with thee. Blessed art thou among women, and blessed is the fruit of thy womb, Jesus. Holy Mary, Mother of God, pray for us sinners, now and at the hour of our death. Amen.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></details><!-- /wp:details --><!-- wp:details --><details class="wp-block-details"><summary>Glory Be</summary><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Glory be to the Father, and to the Son, and to the Holy Spirit. As it was in the beginning, is now, and ever shall be, world without end. Amen.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></details><!-- /wp:details --><!-- wp:details --><details class="wp-block-details"><summary>Hail, Holy Queen</summary><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Hail, Holy Queen, Mother of Mercy, our life, our sweetness, and our hope. To thee do we cry, poor banished children of Eve: to thee do we send up our sighs, mourning and weeping in this valley of tears. Turn then, O most gracious Advocate, thine eyes of mercy toward us, and after this, our exile, show unto us the blessed fruit of thy womb, Jesus. O clement, O loving, O sweet Virgin Mary! Pray for us, O Holy Mother of God, that we may be made worthy of the promises of Christ. Amen.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></details><!-- /wp:details --><!-- wp:details --><details class="wp-block-details"><summary>Concluding prayer</summary><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>O God, whose only begotten Son, by His life, death and Resurrection, has purchased for us the rewards of eternal life; grant, we beseech Thee, that by meditating upon these Mysteries of the Most Holy Rosary of the Blessed Virgin Mary, we may imitate what they contain and obtain what they promise, through the same Christ our Lord. Amen.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></details><!-- /wp:details --><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"fr-source-note"} --><p class="fr-source-note">Prayer texts reproduced from <a class="text-link" href="https://www.familyrosary.org/how-to-pray-the-rosary">Family Rosary’s existing guide</a>.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></section><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:group {"className":"fr-wrap fr-section fr-reading","layout":{"type":"default"},"tagName":"section","anchor":"mysteries"} --><section id="mysteries" class="wp-block-group fr-wrap fr-section fr-reading"><!-- wp:heading {"level":2} --><h2 class="wp-block-heading">Mysteries of the Rosary by day</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The days below follow a common weekly pattern. Sunday customs can vary with the liturgical season; you may choose another set.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:html --><div class="fr-mystery-list"><details><summary>Joyful mysteries <span>Monday and Saturday</span></summary><ol><li>The Annunciation</li><li>The Visitation</li><li>The Nativity</li><li>The Presentation</li><li>The Finding of Jesus in the Temple</li></ol></details><details><summary>Sorrowful mysteries <span>Tuesday and Friday</span></summary><ol><li>The Agony in the Garden</li><li>The Scourging at the Pillar</li><li>The Crowning with Thorns</li><li>The Carrying of the Cross</li><li>The Crucifixion</li></ol></details><details open><summary>Glorious mysteries <span>Wednesday and Sunday</span></summary><ol><li>The Resurrection</li><li>The Ascension</li><li>The Descent of the Holy Spirit</li><li>The Assumption</li><li>The Coronation of Mary</li></ol></details><details><summary>Luminous mysteries <span>Thursday</span></summary><ol><li>The Baptism of Jesus</li><li>The Wedding at Cana</li><li>The Proclamation of the Kingdom</li><li>The Transfiguration</li><li>The Institution of the Eucharist</li></ol></details></div><!-- /wp:html --></section><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:group {"className":"fr-wrap fr-section fr-reading","layout":{"type":"default"},"tagName":"section","anchor":"questions"} --><section id="questions" class="wp-block-group fr-wrap fr-section fr-reading"><!-- wp:heading {"level":2} --><h2 class="wp-block-heading">Questions about praying the Rosary</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:html --><div class="fr-questions"><details><summary>Do I have to know every prayer?</summary><p>No. Read the words from a guide as you go. You can learn the prayers through repetition.</p></details><details><summary>Can I begin with one decade?</summary><p>Yes. A decade gives you a manageable place to begin and learn the rhythm. It is part of the Rosary, not a replacement name for all five decades.</p></details><details><summary>What if my children can’t sit still?</summary><p>Give them a simple role, such as naming an intention or counting a decade. Try a short shared moment and build a routine that your family can grow into.</p></details><details><summary>Where can I find a guide in another language?</summary><p>Read the English prayers on this site, or open the Español and Português PDF guides from our <a class="text-link" href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/rosary-prayer-guide/#language-guides' ) ); ?>">prayer guide language section</a>.</p></details></div><!-- /wp:html --><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"fr-source-note"} --><p class="fr-source-note">Sources for the order and mysteries: <a class="text-link" href="https://www.usccb.org/how-to-pray-the-rosary">USCCB Rosary guide</a> and <a class="text-link" href="https://www.familyrosary.org/how-to-pray-the-rosary">Family Rosary’s existing guide</a>.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></section><!-- /wp:group -->
